## 1. Critical Bugs Found in Current Code

These are functional defects that break existing features and must be resolved before any Phase 2 work.

### BUG-1 — postMessage Namespace Mismatch

**Severity:** P0 — breaks the "Slide X of Y" counter entirely.

The `DeckViewer.vue` listens for:
```js
if (e.data?.namespace === 'reveal') { ... }
```

But every Reveal.js HTML file emits:
```js
window.parent.postMessage({ type: 'slidechanged', totalSlides: ... }, '*')
```

The namespaces never match. The counter will always read `Slide 1 of 0`.

**Fix:**
```js
// DeckViewer.vue — onMounted handler
window.addEventListener('message', (e) => {
  if (e.data?.type === 'slidechanged') {
    slideIndex.value = (e.data.indexh ?? 0) + 1
    slideTotal.value = e.data.totalSlides ?? 0
  }
})
```

| # | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|
| AC-1 | Slide counter displays correct "Slide X of Y" after `slidechanged` event fires from any reveal HTML. |
| AC-2 | Counter resets to "Slide 1 of Y" when a new version is loaded via `VersionSelector`. |
| AC-3 | Slide counter is still shown when `totalSlides` is 0 (loading state). |

---

### BUG-2 — `keepalive` on Wrong Page

**Severity:** P1 — UX regression for back-navigation.

`definePageMeta({ keepalive: true })` is set in `pages/decks/[id].vue`. The PRD (Section 12 UX Recommendations) specifically calls for `keepalive` on the **home page** to preserve scroll position when navigating back from a deck. The current placement keeps the deck viewer alive unnecessarily and doesn't solve the stated UX problem.

| # | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|
| AC-1 | `keepalive: true` removed from `pages/decks/[id].vue`. |
| AC-2 | `definePageMeta({ keepalive: true })` added to `pages/index.vue`. |
| AC-3 | After navigating from the home grid to a deck and pressing browser back, the home page scroll position is restored. |

---

### BUG-3 — Global Keyboard Handler Fires in Search Bar

**Severity:** P1 — typing "f" in the search bar toggles fullscreen.

`DeckViewer.vue` adds a global `keydown` listener that intercepts `ArrowLeft`, `ArrowRight`, and `f`/`F`. This fires even when the user is focused on the `SearchBar` input or any other interactive element.

**Fix:** guard the handler:
```js
function handleKeydown(e: KeyboardEvent) {
  const tag = (e.target as HTMLElement).tagName
  if (tag === 'INPUT' || tag === 'TEXTAREA' || tag === 'SELECT') return
  // ... existing logic
}
```

| # | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|
| AC-1 | Arrow keys in SearchBar input do not navigate slides. |
| AC-2 | Pressing `f` while focused on any text input does not trigger fullscreen. |
| AC-3 | Arrow keys and `f` still work correctly when the iframe viewer is focused. |

---

### BUG-4 — `useRecentDecks` localStorage Called Without SSR Guard

**Severity:** P2 — will throw during SSR/prerender if `localStorage` is accessed.

`addRecent` calls `load()` which calls `localStorage.getItem`. While `onMounted` guards the initial load, `addRecent` can theoretically be called in a non-client context.

**Fix:** Add `if (import.meta.client)` guard in both `load()` and `addRecent()`.

| # | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|
| AC-1 | `nuxt generate` completes without `localStorage is not defined` errors. |
| AC-2 | `addRecent` is a no-op in SSR context. |

---

### BUG-5 — FOUC on Dark Mode (No Inline Head Script)

**Severity:** P2 — flash of unstyled content on hard reload for dark-mode users.

The `plugins/theme.client.ts` plugin runs *after* Vue hydrates — meaning users with `dark` stored in localStorage will briefly see the light theme, then dark applies. The standard fix is an inline `<script>` in `<head>` that runs synchronously.

**Fix:** Add to `nuxt.config.ts`:
```ts
app: {
  head: {
    script: [
      {
        innerHTML: `(function(){var t=localStorage.getItem('sw-theme');if(t==='dark'||(t!=='light'&&matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme:dark)').matches))document.documentElement.classList.add('dark')})()`,
        type: 'text/javascript'
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

| # | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|
| AC-1 | Hard reload in dark mode shows no white flash. |
| AC-2 | Hard reload in light mode shows no dark flash. |
| AC-3 | Script is synchronous and executes before first paint. |

---

## 2. Nuxt Configuration Gaps

### GAP-1 — Missing `routeRules` / Render Strategy

The PRD (Section 7.1) recommends `routeRules` with ISR, but `netlify.toml` uses `npm run generate` (fully static). These are incompatible. A decision is needed.

**Recommendation:** For a speaker slide repo with infrequent updates, **full static generation is correct**. Remove the ISR mention from the PRD and add `routeRules` for prerendering all deck routes at build time.

Add to `nuxt.config.ts`:
```ts
routeRules: {
  '/': { prerender: true },
  '/decks/**': { prerender: true },
}
```

Also add to `netlify.toml`:
```toml
[[redirects]]
  from = "/*"
  to = "/index.html"
  status = 200
```
(Catches any client-side route that Netlify doesn't have a static file for.)

| # | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|
| AC-1 | All deck routes are pre-rendered at build time (`.output/public/decks/{id}/index.html` exists). |
| AC-2 | Netlify redirects ensure direct URL access to `/decks/{id}` works without 404. |
| AC-3 | `nuxt generate` completes in < 90 seconds (performance budget). |
| AC-4 | PRD Section 7.1 updated to remove ISR mention; replaced with prerender strategy. |

