### GAP-17 — Gradient Thumbnails Need Stronger Visual Personality

The current gradients (e.g., `from-emerald-500 to-green-600`) are functional but adjacent colors. Per the frontend-design skill: "What makes this UNFORGETTABLE?"

**Recommendation:** Use contrasting, cross-hue gradients for visual energy:
```ts
// types/index.ts — TAG_COLORS rework
vue:           'from-emerald-400 to-teal-700',
javascript:    'from-amber-400 to-orange-600',
typescript:    'from-sky-400 to-blue-700',
career:        'from-violet-500 to-purple-800',
'soft-skills': 'from-rose-400 to-pink-700',
// ...
```

Also: add a subtle noise texture overlay on each thumbnail for depth:
```css
.card-thumbnail::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,...noise...");
  opacity: 0.06;
  mix-blend-mode: overlay;
}
```

| # | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|
| AC-1 | Each tag has a visually distinct, cross-hue gradient that is immediately differentiable. |
| AC-2 | Gradient pairs pass 3:1 contrast for the white text/icons overlaid on them. |
| AC-3 | Optional: noise overlay adds depth without obscuring tier label. |

